const ARCHIVE_DATA = {"inventory":{"merged":"2026-10-31","authority":"About Eclipsed Realms","records":98,"storyboardBeats":49,"atlasGuides":18,"atlasPriorities":5,"atlasPerformances":16,"images":21,"originalSourceSnapshotsRetainedLocally":74,"sources":{"original":"Eclipsed Realms","storyboard":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","discover":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","atlas":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas"}},"records":[{"id":"original-beginning","title":"The world is a mask.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["Single-player dark fantasy action RPG","The world is a mask.","You survived beneath a house built over the dead. Now every power in the realm has a reason to decide what that survival means.","In development · systems, names and presentation may evolve"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["play-modes","magic","balance"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-premise","title":"A world where every kind of power leaves evidence behind.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["What is Eclipsed Realms?","A world where every kind of power leaves evidence behind.","Eclipsed Realms is an open-zone action RPG about surviving a realm whose religions, monsters, cities and magic all grew around the remains of one ancient failure. Fight with steel, bows, shields, stealth and ritual magic. Build relationships through cruelty, cunning or compassion. Earn trust from factions that do not agree on what salvation looks like. Decide what you are willing to spend—stamina, blood, reputation or permanent corruption—to keep moving.","Weapons, stamina, timing and positioning define the fight.","Holy, Blood and Dark power demand different sacrifices.","Karma, faction standing and personal relationships remember different choices.","Settlements, wilderness and buried spaces share one fractured history."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["ending","magic","personality","balance","lore"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-story","title":"A prison made from six anchors.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"World & story","paragraphs":["I","The Story","A prison made from six anchors.","The story begins with the aftermath of the First Binding: an ancient act of containment whose failure shaped the land long before the player awakened inside it.","The realm inherited the ritual. It did not inherit the whole truth.","Foundational Event","The First Binding","The wound beneath every kingdom","Purpose","Containment","Structure","Six blood anchors","Condition","Fractured","Legacy","Magic leaks through the broken geometry","Six anchors were joined through blood to create a prison for something that could not be destroyed. The Binding transformed place, sacrifice and ritual into a single geometry. For a time, it held.","Then the seal cracked. Its structure remains embedded in the realm, but its purpose no longer functions cleanly. Holy practice, blood rites and dark corruption are separate traditions built around contact with that broken design.","Every major power has inherited a fragment of the truth. None of them can claim the whole of it.","The Ossuary","One of the Cult arena's victims awakens in a pile of bodies beneath an old house near the Start Village. The house predates both the current village and the modern Cult; practitioners of Holy, Blood and Dark rites once used it.","The Relief","The priest finds the Relief after being unknowingly led to it by the Doll. The discovery connects the mystery beneath the house to a form of magic that must be carried, placed and used.","The Six Demons","The Nun summoned the six Greater Flesh Demons in the Cult arena. Captives are forced through them in sequence, turning the arena into an ordeal almost nobody survives—and placing the Nun at the center of the larger demonic story.","The Other Survivor","The Cult claims another person survived and sends the player toward him. The player can approach the encounter as rescue, execution or investigation, but the stranger dies regardless.","The Kingdom","What the player has done—and who is still willing to stand with them—determines whether the Cult, the Kingdom or the Hidden Village can shape the final crisis.","Eclipsed Realms gives the player control over motive, allegiance, relationships and consequence. It does not promise that every death can be prevented or every tragedy can be erased. The stranger's death is fixed; the meaning of that death, what the player learns, and who judges the choice remain variable.","The endings follow the same principle. Faction strength and the player's moral direction determine whether the Cult takes the Kingdom, the Cult is destroyed while the Kingdom remains unchanged, or the Hidden Village is able to help save it."],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","ending","opening","magic","casting","cathedral","balance","lore","demons"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-people","title":"Meet the figures who recognize the survivor.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"World & story","paragraphs":["II","People of the Realm","Meet the figures who recognize the survivor.","Each profile presents what can be known without giving away the revelation at the center of the game.","Custom protagonist · Survivor","The Player","A life the ossuary failed to keep","Origin","Unknown at awakening","Last ordeal","Victim of the Cult arena","Disposition","Cruel · Cunning · Compassionate","Allegiance","Chosen through play","The player was one of the Cult arena's victims and awakens among bodies beneath the old house. Surviving what almost nobody survives turns the protagonist into a question every major power wants answered.","The player begins without a predetermined morality or class. Character creation defines appearance. Weapons, armor, skill investment and Relief choices define how that character acts under pressure.","Dialogue develops three personality traits. Cruel, Cunning and Compassionate answers affect relationships and strengthen the corresponding part of the character's social identity. Clothing can reinforce those traits, making presentation part of the build.","Priest · Start Village","The Priest","The man who finds the Relief","Discovery","Finds the Relief","Conviction","“Murder saves”","Gift","Creates waypoints","Service","Reduces Dark Points while willing","The priest finds the Relief. What he does not understand is that the Doll has led him to it, using his doubt and growing disillusionment to bring an ancient ritual object back into the world.","His crisis hardens into a theology built around the belief that murder saves. Yet his path is not fixed: the player may redeem him, darken him, fight him or still need the old knowledge he carries.","He can create waypoint symbols and remove Dark Points while he remains willing to help. Both services depend on the player's relationship with him.","Former healer · Witch / Nun settlement","The Nun","She summoned the six Greater Flesh Demons","Before","Healer among plague and mass death","Defining act","Summoned the six Greater Flesh Demons","Condition","Stranded between life and death","Before she became the Nun, she was a healer who remained untouched by sickness while tending the dying. Prolonged contact with death and Communion carried her beyond the Veil and left her suspended between states, still wearing the identity of the woman she had been.","She is the one who summoned the six Greater Flesh Demons into the Cult arena. That act makes her far more than the authority who handles karma and repentance: it ties her directly to the ordeal that consumes the arena's captives and to the deeper threat surrounding Demon Father.","Conscious vessel · Dark Communion","The Doll","She is already waiting at the next symbol","Made by","Ancestors of the Hidden Village","Contained","Dark Communion","Known limit","Cannot be defeated at waypoint encounters","Behavior","Controls where confrontation occurs","The ancestors of the Hidden Village once practiced Holy, Blood and Dark Communion. When they realized something within Dark Communion was becoming aware, they isolated it inside the Doll. Then the vessel became conscious.","She now appears where the ancient network touches the present. She leads the Priest to a Relief without revealing her hand, cannot be defeated at waypoint encounters and later moves confrontation to an arena on her own terms.","No confirmed portrait","Stranger · Claimed survivor","The Other Survivor","A choice whose outcome cannot be owned","Connection","Unknown to the player","Source","The Cult's claim","Fate","Dies regardless of approach","The Cult insists another person survived and sends the player to find him. He is a stranger whose existence may explain something about the player—or expose a lie surrounding the original event.","The player can arrive with mercy, violence or suspicion. His death remains inevitable. What changes is the reason the player came, what was learned, and what the decision reveals to every faction watching."],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","ending","opening","magic","casting","personality","cathedral","balance","lore","demons"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-places","title":"Every settlement grew over an older layer.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"World & story","paragraphs":["III","Places","Every settlement grew over an older layer.","The realm moves from lived-in villages and controlled city districts to ritual arenas, flooded underways and structures built for the dead.","Settlement · Early social hub","Start Village","Ordinary life beside an extraordinary grave","Landmark","The old house","Key figure","The priest","Hidden layer","Ossuary","The Start Village grounds the opening in work, worship, neighbors and local loyalties. It is also built beside evidence that the land was used long before the settlement understood itself as a village.","The house above the ossuary predates the present Cult and village. Holy, Blood and Dark practitioners all passed through its history, making the player's origin inseparable from the three traditions that will define the wider journey.","Hidden faction territory","Hidden Village","A faith that survived outside the walls","Modern tradition","Druidic and Holy","Buried history","All three forms of Communion","Political role","Potential ally of the Kingdom","The Hidden Village preserves an alternative culture with its own architecture, armor, rites and understanding of the realm's condition. Its ancestors once knew Holy, Blood and Dark Communion—and created the Doll when they tried to contain the awareness growing inside the Dark.","That history makes the Village more than a clean “good magic” faction. Its people know what the other factions are touching because their own ancestors helped shape the danger. If the player earns the right alliances, they can still become the force capable of helping save the Kingdom.","Kingdom city · Urban open zone","The City","Law above, hunger below","Districts","Upper and Lower","Night rule","Curfew","Below","Prison and sewer routes","The City compresses wealth, law, poverty, military order and decay behind the same walls. Upper and Lower districts create different rhythms and social pressures, while guards enforce a curfew that changes how the streets function after dark.","The City's clean map is incomplete. Its prison reaches downward, the Thieves occupy sewer routes, and older structures complicate every official claim of control.","Gothic settlement · Witch / Nun territory","Cathedral Village","Where repentance becomes authority","Center","Gothic cathedral","Power","Repentance and summoning","Faction","Witch / Nun","The cathedral dominates this settlement both physically and spiritually. Its people follow a severe interpretation of faith, wrongdoing and intervention that does not align neatly with the Start Village priest or the Hidden Village.","The Nun's presence turns the area into more than a place of worship. Her history as a healer, her altered state and her creation of the six arena demons connect this settlement to the story's deepest supernatural conflict.","Cult territory · Ritual settlement","Cultist Village","Forbidden practice made public","Roman-inspired colosseum","Practice","Blood rites and summoning","Threat","Organized Cult power","The Cultist Village is not a scattering of hidden worshippers. It is a territory with infrastructure, memory and enough power to turn ritual into spectacle. Its community has grown into ruins that still carry the weight of an older age.","The colosseum is both landmark and instrument. The Nun's six demons turn it into a lethal sequence for captives; the Doll later mirrors its logic in an arena of her own and chooses where the player must meet her.","Connected subterranean spaces","Beneath the Realm","Sewers, prison, ossuary and dark dungeon","Residents","Thieves and prisoners","Routes","Hidden and unofficial","Spaces","Sewer · Prison · Ossuary · Dark Dungeon","Underground spaces are a second map of the realm. The Thieves turn flooded tunnels into territory. The prison extends the Kingdom's authority below the City. Ossuaries and dark dungeons expose structures that belong to an older order entirely.","Mountain passes and gothic corridors serve as transitions into these harsher spaces, carrying the player away from safe roads and toward the architecture of confinement, death and ritual."],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","ending","opening","magic","cathedral","balance","lore","demons"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-magic","title":"Write the name. Place the symbol. Pay the cost.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["IV","The Three Reliefs","Write the name. Place the symbol. Pay the cost.","Magic is a physical ritual. The player throws a Relief to create an influence zone, summons the Spirit Board, and writes the spell's name in blood before the effect manifests from the Relief.","Carry a Relief","Holy, Blood and Dark Reliefs are separate weapons with separate ability sets.","Claim the ground","Throwing the Relief creates an influence zone roughly twenty feet across.","Write the spell","Letters appear in sequence, turning cast time into a visible ritual.","Accept the cost","The tradition determines whether the spell consumes stamina, health or permanent corruption.","Restoration · Protection · Control","Holy Relief","Survival bought with endurance","Cost","Stamina","Identity","Defensive control","Risk","Leaves the body unable to fight or flee","HealRestore the caster's health.","LockRestrict nearby enemies and create recovery space.","ArmorApply major damage reduction for a limited period.","Full HealCommit to a high-tier restoration.","UltimateChannel extreme protection with healing over time.","Enhancement · Bleeding · Rupture","Blood Relief","Momentum purchased from the body","Health + Stamina","Aggressive pressure","Power makes the caster easier to kill","Blood RainIncrease damage by approximately twenty-five percent.","Area BleedSpread sustained damage through a group.","Drain / RuptureBreak down enemies across an area and reclaim momentum.","Blood MeteorDeliver the tradition's largest direct destructive effect.","UltimateTurn survival resources into overwhelming offense.","Evasion · Force · Control · Summoning","Dark Relief","Immediate power, permanent evidence","Dark Points","Threshold","100 points","Cleansing","A willing priest","InvisibilityDisappear for a cost of 1 Dark Point.","Radial PushbackDisplace nearby enemies for 2 Dark Points.","Control / FearInterfere with enemy will for 3 Dark Points.","Flesh DemonSummon forbidden power for 15 Dark Points.","CorruptionDark Points persist until a willing priest removes them.","Spirit Board","The casting focus is also a weapon.","Summoning the Board changes the character's combat state. Ordinary attacks become close-range strikes, Relief-specific actions replace the usual attack behavior, and the four learned spells sit on the face buttons while the spell modifier is held. LB + RB commits the current ultimate.","Instant spells","One-second lockout","Cast spells","Locked until the cast ends","Relief movement","Recall and throw again","Progression","Four tiers, ultimate and branching passives"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["magic","casting","balance"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-section-6","title":"Every weapon should make danger feel different.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["Combat","Every weapon should make danger feel different."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-combat","title":"Readable, decisive and built around stamina.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["V","Combat & Builds","Readable, decisive and built around stamina.","Combat aims for the physical readability of an action RPG while keeping the freedom to combine weapons, stealth, armor, social traits and magic without selecting a permanent class.","Weapon families","Choose a rhythm, not a label.","One-handed sword and shield, daggers, two-handed weapons, bows and shield-focused play occupy distinct timings and combat roles. A dagger deals less damage per strike but recovers quickly. A bow creates lethal pressure at range. Heavy attacks reward a larger commitment.","Stamina is the combat economy","Attacking, shooting, blocking and dodging all draw from the same resource. Capacity and regeneration shape how long any martial style can control a fight.","Damage remains legible","The current baseline begins around 100 player health. Representative values place a medium one-handed light hit near 55, a heavy hit near 85 and a bow hit near 70, keeping individual attacks meaningful.","Recovery requires action","Health persists after combat. Food and drink restore it over time, water supports stamina, brewed drinks offer regeneration or resistance, and Holy magic provides immediate recovery at a stamina cost.","Defense is timing","Blocking and dodging protect through resource management and timing. A shield-parry concept adds a narrow stagger window for players who commit to precise defense.","Stealth & Critical Strikes","Critical chance accelerates near mastery.","Stealth feeds a deliberately skewed critical curve. Early investment produces modest gains; the increase becomes more pronounced near 100 stealth. The target cap is 35% critical chance at 100 stealth with 1.5× critical damage.","Crouching adds 5 stealth.","Stealth Training has five ranks, each adding 10 stealth.","Thief gear adds 2 stealth per piece; caster gear adds 1 per piece.","Knight, Templar and Guard armor impose increasingly serious stealth penalties.","Armor & Equipment","Mixed sets are part of the build.","Bonuses are applied per piece across five equipment slots. A player can combine Knight plate, Druid equipment, Thief leather and caster pieces instead of waiting for a complete-set rule to recognize the build.","Each Druid piece targets +20% maximum stamina and +10% stamina regeneration.","Thief pieces add direct stealth support.","Caster pieces provide a lighter stealth contribution.","Military armor trades concealment for direct combat identity.","Progression","The world scales selectively.","Levels run from 1 to 100, with the broader health curve moving from roughly 100 HP toward 1000 HP. Rewards account for enemy level and difficulty, targeting approximately ten appropriate fights per level.","Combat, Sneak, Speech and Fortitude form the core skills.","Trash, mid-tier and boss enemies use increasing reward multipliers.","Dungeons scale to remain relevant.","Ambient low-level enemies remain weak enough to show the player's growth.","Controller language","Combat stays under the player's hands.","The standard layout keeps defense, attacks, interaction and movement consistent while the Spirit Board changes the meaning of combat inputs when it is equipped.","LT","Block","RT","Light / Heavy attack","LB","Ability wheel","RB","Special action","LB + RB","Ultimate","Y","Charge / summon Board by context","X · A · B","Interact · Jump · Crouch","D-pad","Inventory left · Map right","With the Spirit Board active, the face buttons become the learned Relief spells while the spell modifier is held; ordinary attack inputs become punches and Relief-specific actions."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["magic","casting","balance"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-factions","title":"No single score can explain who trusts you.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"World & story","paragraphs":["VI","Factions & Consequence","No single score can explain who trusts you.","Karma, faction reputation and personal relationships track different kinds of consequence. Helping a faction can still be cruel. Acting compassionately can still create an enemy.","Karma","A negative-to-positive record of broad moral consequence. Extreme positions affect judgment, access and hostility. The nun's repentance addresses this burden.","Faction Standing","Separate reputations for the Start Village, Hidden Village, Cult, Kingdom and Witch / Nun faction. Extremes can lead to bans, hostility or privileged access.","Relationships","Individual people respond to the personality and history of the player. Matching their preferred disposition strengthens the bond; repeated mismatch can damage it.","Home","Start Village","Villagers, local loyalties and the priest who connects everyday life to the ancient waypoint network.","Values","Community · Survival · Local trust","Risk","Losing the first place willing to shelter you","Hidden","Druids & Holy Tradition","A culture outside Kingdom authority whose endurance and old knowledge can become decisive in the final conflict.","Old faith · Nature · Endurance","Reward","A powerful ally for the Kingdom's survival","Cult","The Cult","An organized power that treats bloodshed as devotion and the arena as proof of strength. It inherited dangerous rites without understanding every force behind them.","Creed","Blood wins favor · Strength proves worth","Ambition","Control of the Kingdom","Kingdom","Crown, Guards & Citizens","The realm's civic and military authority: nobles above, labor below, guards in the streets and a prison beneath them all.","Order · Law · Continuity","Weakness","Institutions built over truths they do not control","Witch / Nun","The Cathedral Authority","A severe religious power shaped by the Nun's passage from healer to something caught between life and death.","Center","Gothic Cathedral","Service","Karma repentance","Thieves","The Thieves","A criminal faction built around routes, rooms and knowledge the Kingdom cannot fully patrol.","Access · Secrecy · Survival","Territory","The sewer network"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","ending","magic","personality","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-threats","title":"The realm's violence has human and inhuman faces.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"World & story","paragraphs":["VII","Enemies & Threats","The realm's violence has human and inhuman faces.","Some threats are creatures shaped by the realm's corruption. Others are people defending territory, enforcing law or following an allegiance the player has chosen to oppose.","When the trees go quiet, the silhouette is already close.","Wilderness predator · Inhuman threat","Wendigos","Antlered horrors beyond the safe roads","Range","Forests and ruined wilds","Known lair","Wendigo cave","Silhouette","Tall, horned and unmistakable","Encounter","Close-range wilderness threat","Relief link","Blood","Wendigos are among the realm's defining nonhuman enemies: towering, antlered predators that turn travel through the forest into an encounter with something physically overwhelming.","Their cave is tied to the discovery of the Blood Relief, binding this creature threat directly to the player's magical progression rather than leaving it as a detached wilderness encounter.","The Cult arena","The Six Demons","The Nun summoned all six Greater Flesh Demons. Once-human vessels, they have been fed by the arena's repeated deaths across generations. The Cult forces captives through them in sequence, and almost nobody survives the full ordeal.","Made through Communion","Flesh Demons","Lesser and Greater forms are created through forbidden practice. Lesser forms can eventually be summoned by the player; the Greater forms define the arena's major confrontations.","Human ritualists","Cultists","Their creed makes killing an act of devotion and survival proof of worth. Their danger comes from organization, blood rites and confidence that sacrifice earns favor.","Wilderness","Corrupted Beasts","Forest life reshaped into grotesque evidence that the realm's corruption reaches beyond human belief.","Conditional hostility","Druids","The Hidden Village can stand beside the player or against them. Conflict grows from choices, reputation and territory—not from a blanket rule that every faction is an enemy.","Law and military power","Knights & Guards","The Kingdom's armed authority enforces its streets, borders and curfew. Whether they are protectors or opponents depends on what the player has done.","Under-city faction","Thieves","The sewer network gives the Thieves routes, concealment and territory beyond the Kingdom's cleanest maps."],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","ending","magic","casting","cathedral","balance","lore","demons"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-worldplay","title":"Travel, time and preparation carry consequences too.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["VIII","The Living World","Travel, time and preparation carry consequences too.","Exploration connects open zones, settlements, dungeons and transitional spaces while keeping repeated travel generous once the player has earned familiarity with a route.","Day & Night","The world keeps a longer rhythm.","The cycle uses a 14-hour daylight and 10-hour night proportion, stretched so the sun's movement feels gradual. Darkness changes more than lighting: the City's curfew alters access, safety and the meaning of being outside after hours.","Ancient symbols become a modern road.","Discovered waypoints allow unlimited fast travel. The Start Village priest can create new symbols, connecting a convenience system directly to the lore of the broken Binding.","Roads still matter before they become familiar.","A mount supports long distances. Swimming, ladders and cover open alternate paths through settlements, wilderness and interiors. Indoor and outdoor navigation share the minimap system.","Challenge lives where it belongs.","Dungeons scale and respawnable challenge spaces preserve difficult combat. Ambient low-tier enemies remain low enough for progression to feel real.","What you carry changes the next fight.","Food heals over time. Water supports stamina. Brewed drinks add regeneration and resistance. Relief choice, armor pieces and weapon family determine which risks the player is prepared to take."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["travel","magic","casting","balance","lore"],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-gallery","title":"Places, rituals and nightmares.","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["IX","Visual Archive","Places, rituals and nightmares.","Concept imagery and visual development for the atmosphere, people and creatures of Eclipsed Realms."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":[],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"original-section-12","title":"Closing words","source":"original","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["The seal is broken. Every road leads through what escaped."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":[],"notes":["September 19, 2026 · published version 3","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"discover-view-overview","title":"Eclipsed Realms","source":"discover","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["A dark fantasy co-op action RPG","Eclipsed Realms","Save a fractured world. Or claim what remains.","Awaken with broken memories in a realm where faith, blood and forbidden power shape more than the next battle.","Cult cathedralSupplied environment reference","The choice is yours","A story of good, evil, and the price of becoming either.","Fight your way to the top or stand against the corruption consuming the world. Explore open-world zones, build relationships, choose your loyalties and shape your character through action, magic and personality.","The seal is broken.","The First Binding, the Cult, hidden villages, the kingdom and the people who inhabit them.","Build your approach.","Weapons, defense, techniques, attributes, personality, skills and character progression.","Choose your power.","All fifteen spells, upgrades, deployment rules, ultimate abilities and the cost of corruption.","Leave your mark.","Personal relationships, faction reputation, karma, witnesses and meaningful quest decisions.","Face the dark together.","Campaign co-op, dungeon companions, the Cursed Doll’s training and competitive arenas.","See the realm.","Explore the supplied cathedral images at full size, with their original details preserved.","A dark fantasy action RPG with open-world zones, co-op, Relief-based magic and consequential choices. Relationships, faction reputation, karma and corruption are central parts of its design.","Eclipsed Realms is in development. Release timing and final supported configurations will be shared as the project progresses.","The cathedral images are supplied environment asset references. They show the visual material selected for the realm, rather than an invented concept location or a capture of final gameplay."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["play-modes","travel","ending","magic","casting","personality","cathedral","targets","balance","lore"],"notes":["October 9, 2026 · published version 2","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"discover-view-world","title":"The seal is broken. The reckoning begins.","source":"discover","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","category":"World & story","paragraphs":["01 / World & story","The seal is broken. The reckoning begins.","You awaken in a torture dungeon, a survivor of the Cult’s machinery. Your memories are fragments. Beyond the walls, an ancient seal has fractured—and magic is leaking into the world.","The First Binding","A prison made with blood.","The First Binding failed. Six anchors formed a prison, but its seal could not hold. What escaped now reaches into places, people and the powers they wield.","Your journey begins among the consequences of that failure. The choice is whether to resist the corruption—or use it.","The cathedral approachSupplied environment reference","The opening village","The first settlement beyond your escape. Meet its people and begin to understand the world you have returned to.","The Hidden Village","A secluded community tied to Druid and Holy traditions, with the Old Man and his family at the heart of its stories.","Cult territory","Dark Relief users, a colosseum and the cathedral. The Cult’s reach extends well beyond the dungeon where you awaken.","The kingdom","Upper and lower districts, royal power, guards, curfew and a prison. What the city permits is not always what it forgives.","The Witch Priest’s village","A settlement connected to the healer known as the Witch Priest, with its own people, beliefs and place in the story.","The sewers","Below the city, the thieves have their own territory and loyalties. The kingdom looks different from underneath.","The Cursed Doll","A strange guide bound to ancient symbols. Her role reaches into travel, Dark Communion and the Training Arena.","Main Priest","A Holy figure connected to Relief magic and the waypoints that help you navigate the realm.","Witch Priest","A plague-resistant healer whose place in the main story extends far beyond a single village.","The Old Man","A Holy Relief user in the Hidden Village. His trust opens the way to deeper lessons.","The royal court","King Melato, Queen Sicilian and the kingdom’s Blood mage occupy the center of royal power.","The Jester","At the Opera Hall, completed quests can become performances—stories you may step into again.","A story to discover","Follow a crying boy through the forest. Earn the Old Man’s trust. Learn why the Doll is waiting. The people you encounter lead you into quests whose full consequences belong in the game."],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","ending","opening","magic","casting","jester","cathedral","balance","lore"],"notes":["October 9, 2026 · published version 2","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"discover-view-gameplay","title":"Steel when words fail. A character shaped by you.","source":"discover","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["02 / Combat & character growth","Steel when words fail. A character shaped by you.","Build a fighting style around your weapons, techniques and Relief school. Choose your starting attributes and personality, then grow through skills and upgrades.","Make the opening.","Close-range attacks, bows and Relief magic offer different approaches to an encounter. Weapon techniques give you a dedicated move beyond the basic attack.","Defend with intent.","Blocking relies on stamina. A well-timed shield parry can stagger an opponent and create a chance to act.","Read the enemy.","Face ordinary enemies, bosses and elites. More dangerous opponents can change their pace as a fight turns against them.","Weapon · Its advantage","Sword · Armor penetration.","Axe · Greater bleed potential.","Dagger · Increased critical damage.","Shield · Reduced bleed taken, alongside blocking and parrying.","Two-handed weapons · Stronger versions of the corresponding weapon passive.","Begin with choices. Grow into a style.","Choose your appearance, allocate twelve starting attribute points and give your personality a head start with fifteen points in five-point steps.","Your starting selections support the character you want to play. They are followed by skill unlocks, techniques, spell upgrades and continued character growth.","Strength","Improves attack power.","Dexterity","Improves stealth.","Intelligence","Improves maximum stamina.","Vitality","Improves maximum health.","Charisma","Improves your initial standing with people and factions.","Witty","Give your character a sharper voice in conversations.","Empathetic","Make understanding others part of your approach.","Bold","Meet a conversation with confidence and willingness to take a risk.","Personality helps shape dialogue options. Some conversations offer an additional risky response.","Skills & progression","Spend points on skills, techniques and Relief abilities. New Game+ and New Game++ extend the journey and its character growth.","Equipment & survival","Manage weapons, armor, food, water and other carried items. Health, stamina, armor, attack power, stealth and critical stats inform your build.","Travel & rest","Discover waypoints, travel on foot or on horseback, and use campsites to rest, eat, save or load before continuing."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["travel","magic","casting","personality","targets","balance"],"notes":["October 9, 2026 · published version 2","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"discover-view-magic","title":"Three Reliefs. Three ways to change the fight.","source":"discover","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["Three Reliefs. Three ways to change the fight.","Magic begins with a Relief. Wield it, deploy it, and step inside its influence to cast. Each Relief can serve one caster at a time.","The Holy Relief","A light worth holding onto.","Restore health, reinforce your defenses and hold enemies in place. Holy magic gives you the strength to endure—and the means to help others endure beside you.","Lesser Heal","A quick restoration of health.","20% → 35% health restored","Greater Heal","More powerful healing when the fight demands it.","45% → 80% health restored","Holy Armor","Strengthen your armor for the struggle ahead.","+300 → +500 armor · 20 seconds","Binding Light","Root an enemy and reclaim the moment.","5 → 8 seconds of rooting","Divine Renewal","Recover health over time.","8% → 15% health restored per second","The Blood Relief","Power always asks for something.","Turn sacrifice into strength. Drain life, surge into battle and command a demon to fight beside you. Blood magic rewards those willing to pay its price.","Offering","Trade health for greater attack power and armor.","30 → 45 seconds · attack power and armor improve","Siphon","Drain life from your enemy.","A 5-second channel · life drain improves with upgrades","Rush","Move faster and seize the opening.","+25% → +45% movement speed · 15 seconds","Rupture","Unleash damage along a forward lane.","150% → 275% of attack power","Summon Demon","Call a temporary demonic ally into the fight.","45 seconds · upgraded demon gains 75% health and damage","The Dark Relief","Let the darkness in. Feel what it takes.","Disappear from sight, turn fear against your enemies and leave them marked by a curse. Dark spells build Dark Points. At full corruption, your health and stamina suffer, and you can no longer cast Holy magic.","Invisibility","Conceal yourself from sight.","10 → 15 seconds · upgrade adds healing","Void Pulse","Push enemies away and create space.","5 → 8 meters of knockback","Fear","Send your enemy into terror.","5 → 9 seconds of fear","Curse","Wear an enemy down with damage over time.","20% → 35% of target maximum health as damage over time","Dark Continuance","Draw on the Dark for a temporary increase in power.","10 → 20 seconds · +15% → +25% attack power","Each school has five spells to unlock and upgrade, plus an ultimate ability. Values shown describe the current design and may be tuned during development.","Wield & deploy.","The appropriate Relief must be wielded to grant its abilities. Deploy it and remain within its influence to cast.","One caster at a time.","A deployed Relief serves a single user. Its influence is a place you must manage in the fight.","Commit at release.","Letters are written over the Relief as you cast. The cost and cooldown begin when the completed cast visibly releases. An interrupted cast that never releases does not spend them.","Dark Points","Power leaves a mark.","Dark spells add Dark Points. At one hundred, corruption reduces maximum health, maximum stamina and stamina regeneration by ten percent, and prevents Holy casting.","Main Priest can help reduce Dark Points. Corruption is distinct from karma: the magic you use and the choices you make are different parts of your character.","Ultimate abilities","Each Relief school has an ultimate to unlock. Learning and improving magic is part of progression through the people and quests of the realm."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["ending","magic","casting","balance","lore"],"notes":["October 9, 2026 · published version 2","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"discover-view-choices","title":"The world remembers who you become.","source":"discover","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["04 / Choices & consequences","The world remembers who you become.","Trust, reputation, karma and corruption each track a different part of your journey. A person’s opinion of you is not interchangeable with a faction’s standing—or with the power you carry.","Trust is personal.","Each NPC can have a relationship with you. Your actions and conversations can earn their trust or give them a reason to doubt you, changing how they respond.","Loyalties carry weight.","Factions have their own standing with you. Helping one group may not make you welcome among another, and the people you encounter have reasons for their loyalties.","Your path is yours.","Karma follows your moral choices. The route toward saving the realm and the pursuit of corrupt power lead the story in different directions.","What was seen can matter later.","The consequence system accounts for witnessed actions. NPC reactions can reflect what they know, rather than treating every encounter as a fresh start.","Starting an assault and defending yourself are different situations. The design also accounts for NPC aggression toward the player.","Guards, arrest & jail","Guard responses and arrest/jail behavior are part of the consequence-system work. They extend the relationship between an incident, its witnesses and the people responsible for keeping order.","Earn the next step.","A mentor’s trust can be the difference between meeting them and learning what they have to teach.","Choose how to respond.","Personality gives conversations different voices. A witty answer, an empathetic reply or a bold response can shape the way an encounter unfolds.","Live with the result.","Quest decisions can change your path, the relationships around you and what comes next. The full outcomes belong in the story you play.","Karma & Dark Points","Karma concerns your choices. Dark Points concern your use of Dark magic. They are separate systems, each with its own consequences."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["ending","magic","personality","balance","lore"],"notes":["October 9, 2026 · published version 2","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"discover-view-multiplayer","title":"Someone at your side. Someone across the arena.","source":"discover","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["05 / Co-op, companions & arenas","Someone at your side. Someone across the arena.","Campaign co-op, dungeon allies, training and competitive arenas offer different ways to share the realm. The configurations below describe the multiplayer design targets while development continues.","Online campaign players","Explore and fight together in a campaign designed to support up to four online players.","Local co-op players","Two-player couch co-op shares the journey on the same screen.","Two households","The combined target brings two local players together with two local players online.","Final supported configurations will be confirmed as the multiplayer implementation is validated.","Four-player dungeons. More ways to find company.","Dungeons are designed around a group of four. Optional NPC helpers provide a melee fighter, a ranged fighter and a magic user, and can accompany you inside the dungeon.","Helpers join the party for the run, with their health and portrait visible. They leave after the boss is defeated or when you leave through the entrance or exit.","Three roles","Melee: a fighter for close-range pressure.","Ranged: support from a distance.","Magic: a caster alongside the group.","Dungeon allies support the run alongside your player companions.","Learn the enemies. Return to your journey.","Find the Cursed Doll near discovered waypoints and travel to the Training Arena. Practice against enemies associated with the area you came from, one at a time.","Training grants experience but no loot. Return to your origin, or travel to an origin you have already discovered through the Doll.","01Find the DollReach her in an area tied to a waypoint.","02Enter trainingFace that area’s enemies in sequence.","03Return or travelLeave for your origin or a previously discovered one.","A duel","Two-player teams","Three-player teams","Up to eight players","Competitive fights use arena sessions rather than replacing the campaign journey.","A quest becomes a performance.","Replay a completed main quest as a staged performance. The crowd may cheer or boo, but the replay carries no campaign consequences and awards no experience or loot.","Leave the performance and return to the stage when you are ready to continue your real journey."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["play-modes","travel","magic","jester","targets","balance","lore"],"notes":["October 9, 2026 · published version 2","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"discover-view-gallery","title":"The cathedral within the rock.","source":"discover","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","category":"Earlier game design","paragraphs":["06 / Gallery","The cathedral within the rock.","The cult cathedral’s visual reference: gothic stonework, a narrow bridge, steep rock walls and pale light from above.","Facade & entranceSupplied reference","Bridge & approachSupplied reference","These are supplied environment asset references, rather than Eclipsed Realms gameplay captures. Their original watermarks and image contents are preserved."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["cathedral"],"notes":["October 9, 2026 · published version 2","Preserved from the older site. Read the current-rule notes before treating any claim as current."]},{"id":"story-binding","title":"The First Binding","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Six blood-made anchors form a prison. When the Binding fractures, reality—not merely the prison—is damaged.","Story purpose: Establishes the single wound beneath the setting. Death, grief, bones, and memory now thin the boundary.","Continuity:","The prison did not simply open.","Ancient structures remain embedded throughout the land.","The First Binding cannot simply be undone.","Connected threads: Communion, Veil"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Ancient history","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-communion","title":"Communion","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Holy, Blood, and Dark are three approaches to the same wound in reality.","Story purpose: Unifies the magic system: a Relief creates a place where spell names written in blood can answer.","Continuity:","Holy costs stamina.","Blood costs stamina and life.","Dark stores its price inside the user as corruption.","Connected threads: Communion, Reliefs"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Supernatural rule","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-doll","title":"The Vessel Becomes the Doll","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The ancestors separate Dark Communion from Holy and Blood and contain it inside a vessel.","Story purpose: Makes the Doll a consequence of fearful containment rather than a possessed child.","Continuity:","Listening becomes memory, then preference, then will.","The Doll is Dark Communion contained.","She is not Demon Father.","Connected threads: Doll, Hidden Village"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Ancient history","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-doll-plan","title":"The Doll Learns What Blood Does","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Doll learns that fighting, sacrifice, murder, and death feed Communion.","Story purpose: Creates an antagonist who can truthfully help while guiding the world toward violence.","Continuity:","She need not personally kill.","She can warn, transport, and teach.","Repeatable waypoint battles still serve her.","Connected threads: Doll, Cult"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Antagonist thread","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-waypoints","title":"The Ancient Waypoints","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Occult symbols form a travel network older than the modern Cult.","Story purpose: Connects travel, the Doll’s appearances, and repeatable combat to one ancient infrastructure.","Continuity:","The Cult uses but did not create them.","The Doll is effectively untouchable there.","The Priest eventually creates new symbols.","Connected threads: Doll, Priest, Travel"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · World system","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-house","title":"Start House & Buried Practice","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The old house conceals markings and burial spaces from the age when all three Communions were understood together.","Story purpose: Places ancient supernatural history beneath apparently ordinary architecture.","Continuity:","The house predates village and Cult.","The dead were kept close deliberately.","The house, ossuary, and Torture Dungeon are distinct places.","Connected threads: Start Village, Communion"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["opening","lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Location history","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-priest-relief","title":"The Priest Finds the Relief","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The disillusioned Priest is guided to a ruined shoreline where a Relief lies as though waiting for him.","Story purpose: Begins his supernatural certainty without making him part of an established magical order.","Continuity:","He touches it and the Doll appears.","The Relief validates his existing faith.","It is not the player’s Dark Relief.","Connected threads: Priest, Doll"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Historical scene","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-murder-saves","title":"Murder Saves","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A real response from beyond reality becomes proof, to the Priest, that death feeds God.","Story purpose: Builds a catastrophic doctrine from a genuine mechanism and a false explanation.","Continuity:","Something truly receives the energy.","He has mistaken what it is.","Murder becomes sacrifice, devotion, then salvation.","Connected threads: Priest, Start Village"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Belief transformation","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-nun-healer","title":"The Nun Before the Demons","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A disease-resistant healer stays beside plague victims and witnesses the threshold of death repeatedly.","Story purpose: Roots her transformation in compassion, sickness, and prolonged contact with the dying.","Continuity:","Death stops looking final.","She crosses too deeply.","She becomes stranded between living and dead.","Connected threads: Nun, Plague"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Historical thread","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-nun-return","title":"The Priest Summons the Nun","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Doll moves events through the Priest until he brings the Nun back into the story.","Story purpose: Joins Start Village directly to the larger demonic chain.","Continuity:","She briefly appears as the healer and nun she was.","The Priest believes it sacred.","The deeper purpose reasserts itself.","Connected threads: Nun, Priest, Doll"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Before the Player · Historical scene","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-wake","title":"Awakening in the Torture Dungeon","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The player wakes imprisoned, brutalized, and unable to remember why they survived.","Story purpose: Begins with survival and missing identity rather than chosen-hero destiny.","Continuity:","The Torture Dungeon is its own place.","The player had been expected to die.","Escape begins reconstruction of the forgotten ordeal.","Connected threads: Player, Cult"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["opening","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Survival · Playable opening","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-survivor","title":"The Impossible Survivor","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Living through circumstances meant to kill them draws the attention of factions.","Story purpose: Makes the protagonist consequential because of an impossible outcome.","Continuity:","The Priest notices.","The Cult has reason to care.","Rumors spread that someone survived.","Connected threads: Player, Priest, Cult"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Survival · Inciting consequence","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-start-village","title":"The Start Village","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Work, worship, and trade conceal a community changing under the Priest’s doctrine.","Story purpose: Shows ordinary people becoming capable of violence because they believe murder feeds God.","Continuity:","The village does not understand its buried history.","Initiates guard the ossuary.","The Priest can create new waypoints.","Connected threads: Start Village, Priest"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","opening","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Survival · Playable region","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-mutants","title":"Mutant Animals","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Mutant goats and wildlife show that supernatural damage has entered the biological world.","Story purpose: Signals the Nun’s influence before its cause is understood.","Continuity:","They are not generic fantasy wildlife.","The mutations are permanent.","There is no purification reset.","Connected threads: Nun, Forest"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Survival · Environmental reveal","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-abandoned","title":"Abandoned Village & Hybrids","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Animal hybrids and bodies that no longer fit ordinary species define an abandoned settlement.","Story purpose: Escalates mutation into a collapse of human, animal, and monster categories.","Continuity:","Hybrids are distinct from mutant wildlife.","The village is not empty scenery.","Its creatures are part of its identity.","Connected threads: Hybrids, Forest"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Act I · Survival · Playable region","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-forest","title":"The Forest","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Wendigos, Changelings, old churches, caves, and divided paths make the Forest a region in its own right.","Story purpose: Shows that the world outside settlements is changing, not merely dangerous.","Continuity:","Forest Church is separate from Crossroads Church.","Minotaur and Demon Goat Man are distinct encounters.","Routes lead toward the Hidden Village and Reliefs.","Connected threads: Forest, Wendigos, Changelings"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Survival · Playable region","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-hidden","title":"The Hidden Village","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A remote community preserves Communion knowledge and the guilt of ancestors who created the Doll.","Story purpose: Makes the group with the deepest guilt the best human force to resist Demon Father.","Continuity:","Their ancestry includes all three Communions.","They now align strongly with Holy.","Their nearby mountain routes contain the Holy Relief history.","Connected threads: Hidden Village, Holy, Doll"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Playable region","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-old-man","title":"The Old Man’s Grief","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["After his magic harms his wife and she later dies, the Old Man abandons using power.","Story purpose: Creates one answer to dangerous power: withdrawal.","Continuity:","His daughters maintain much of the village.","He retains deep magical knowledge.","Private grief becomes political structure.","Connected threads: Old Man, Hidden Village"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Character history","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-mage","title":"The Son Chooses Mastery","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The son sees the same death and decides ignorance—not magic—was the danger.","Story purpose: Creates the opposing answer: complete mastery used for protection.","Continuity:","He pursues Blood Communion.","He killed a Wendigo on his path.","He becomes royal protector.","Connected threads: Mage, Blood, Kingdom"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Character history","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-holy","title":"The Holy Relief","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The player ascends through the mountain route and older dungeon associated with the Hidden Village.","Story purpose: Connects Holy Communion to the Old Man’s family and local preserved knowledge.","Continuity:","Holy consumes stamina.","The ascent belongs to the Hidden Village region.","The Old Man’s history is closely tied to it.","Connected threads: Holy, Hidden Village"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Relief quest","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-blood","title":"Wendigo Cave & Blood Relief","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The route to Blood Communion passes through Wendigo territory and the Mage’s earlier path.","Story purpose: Connects acquiring Blood power to the son’s belief in mastery.","Continuity:","Blood costs stamina and health.","The Mage killed a Wendigo here.","The cave carries evidence of his journey.","Connected threads: Blood, Wendigos, Mage"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Relief quest","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-kingdom","title":"The Kingdom Under Fear","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A once-liked King taxes heavily to build an army; emergency defense hardens into martial law.","Story purpose: Creates a political conflict where protection and oppression grow from the same decision.","Continuity:","Upper City is insulated.","Lower City feels guards, curfew, and taxation.","The City remains prosperous while resentment rises.","Connected threads: Kingdom, King"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Playable region","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-royal","title":"The Royal Family’s Shield","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Mage makes himself, the King, and the Queen effectively invulnerable.","Story purpose: Physically joins Hidden Village family history to royal politics.","Continuity:","The throne cannot simply be taken with a sword.","The protector is the Old Man’s son.","His goal remains protection rather than conquest.","Connected threads: Kingdom, Mage"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Political obstacle","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-under-city","title":"Prison, Sewers & City Life","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Institutional violence fills the prison while Thieves control unofficial routes below the City.","Story purpose: Shows different forms of power without declaring resistance automatically heroic.","Continuity:","The Thieves can be bribed, befriended, or fought.","The Jester opens distinct quests.","The Opera Hall makes the City culturally alive.","Connected threads: Kingdom, Thieves"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Playable subregions","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-witch","title":"Witch / Nun Region","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Swamps, plague doctors, occult healing, Gothic Cathedral, and Gothic Corridor preserve the Nun’s human origin.","Story purpose: Gives her transformation a lived region rooted in sickness and failed treatment.","Continuity:","Plague shaped the community.","The Cathedral is a major landmark.","The Corridor deepens its religious history.","Connected threads: Nun, Plague"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Powers · Playable region","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-cult","title":"The Cult Village","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A functioning settlement normalizes bloodshed and ritual as ordinary life.","Story purpose: Makes the Cult a society with worship and tradition, not only enemies.","Continuity:","Forgotten Echoes is its church.","The Shaman holds deliberate ritual knowledge.","The Cult inherited rather than invented Communion.","Connected threads: Cult, Doll"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Descent · Playable region","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-dark","title":"The Dark Relief","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The player descends through the Dark Dungeon to forbidden Communion deliberately preserved.","Story purpose: Makes using Dark power a conscious step toward practices witnessed from outside.","Continuity:","This is separate from the Priest’s anomalous Relief.","Dark Points are independent of Karma.","Lesser Flesh Demons can become temporary summons.","Connected threads: Dark, Cult"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Descent · Relief quest","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-memories","title":"The Nun’s Memories","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Reality shifts and the player witnesses moments they were never present for and cannot alter.","Story purpose: Builds the Nun’s story without turning her into a recurring boss.","Continuity:","The player barely meets her normally.","The present returns afterward.","These are memories, not time travel.","Connected threads: Nun, Memory"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Descent · Narrative device","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-attic","title":"The Attic Memory","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The player witnesses the Nun inside a past summoning event in an attic.","Story purpose: Establishes the memory grammar later used in the Arena.","Continuity:","The ritual cannot be prevented.","The Nun is not fought.","The room remains when the past vanishes.","Connected threads: Nun, Memory"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["opening","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Descent · Memory scene","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-other","title":"The Other Survivor","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The player may approach intending rescue, murder, or investigation. He dies regardless.","Story purpose: Makes agency about intention, knowledge, relationship, and identity.","Continuity:","What the player tried still matters.","Others’ opinions can change.","Not every death exists to be prevented.","Connected threads: Player, Cult"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · Descent · Fixed event / variable intent","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-arena-entry","title":"The Empty Cult Arena","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The silent Colosseum contains only the Nun. Entering begins the memory.","Story purpose: Turns the Arena’s origin into something witnessed before the player becomes its next spectacle.","Continuity:","She does not attack.","There is no crowd at first.","This is not the End Church.","Connected threads: Arena, Nun"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · The Arena · Major sequence","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-six","title":"The Six Are Summoned","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Nun summons all six Greater Flesh Demons and dies after the sixth.","Story purpose: Reveals the act around which generations of Arena violence were built.","Continuity:","The event cannot be changed.","The Six are tied to ancient human vessels.","Arena deaths have strengthened them.","Connected threads: Arena, Nun, Demons"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore","demons"],"notes":["Act I · The Arena · Memory climax","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-arena-fight","title":"The Arena Returns to the Present","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Nun vanishes, exits lock, Cultists fill the stands, and the Six enter one at a time.","Story purpose: Makes the player endure the spectacle that killed countless victims.","Continuity:","An Announcer frames the executions.","All six are fought sequentially.","Different factions may want the same outcome for different reasons.","Connected threads: Arena, Cult, Demons"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · The Arena · Major combat","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-after-six","title":"After the Six","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The player survives the Arena, but the final confrontation has not begun.","Story purpose: Keeps two late-game climaxes distinct.","Continuity:","Killing the Six does not summon Demon Father.","The Doll does not transform.","The Nun is not an Arena boss.","Connected threads: Arena, Demon Father"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · The Arena · Transition","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-ossuary","title":"Return Through the Ossuary","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The player crosses the buried beginning again, now understanding the Doll, Priest, Nun, Cult, and Reliefs.","Story purpose: Turns repetition of place into transformation of meaning.","Continuity:","The ossuary is part of the route to the end.","Confusion becomes informed dread.","The End Church still lies ahead.","Connected threads: Ossuary, Player"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","opening","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · End Church · Final approach","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-end-church","title":"The End Church","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Accumulated death has prepared the church. The Nun waits inside, kneeling.","Story purpose: Makes the final ritual the result of power gathering across the story.","Continuity:","The Nun does not attack.","Approaching begins the cinematic.","The place has been filling through death.","Connected threads: Nun, Demon Father"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · End Church · Final location","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-sacrifice","title":"The Nun’s Final Sacrifice","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Nun sacrifices herself and allows Demon Father to exist.","Story purpose: Completes her path from healer beside the dying to final sacrifice beyond death.","Continuity:","She is not the final boss.","She does not become an ordinary monster.","This is separate from summoning the Six.","Connected threads: Nun, Demon Father"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · End Church · Final cinematic","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-father","title":"Demon Father Manifests","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A massive being emerges where the Binding, Communion, Priest, killings, Cult, Six, and Nun converge.","Story purpose: Pays off the supernatural chain without collapsing its distinct figures together.","Continuity:","He is not the Doll.","He is not the Nun or one of the Six.","“Time. A pestilent inconvenience… I have risen.”","Connected threads: Demon Father, Doll, Nun"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Act I · End Church · Final confrontation","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-alliance","title":"Knowledge & Army","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Hidden Village contributes supernatural knowledge; the Kingdom contributes military strength.","Story purpose: Allows tense cooperation without erasing either faction’s failures.","Continuity:","King and Queen may assist.","Guards and knights may join.","Guilt and oppression remain real.","Connected threads: Hidden Village, Kingdom"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · End Church · Ending alliance","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-dark-end","title":"The Darker Path","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The player embraces darker forces and turns the final conflict toward the Kingdom.","Story purpose: Makes dark victory visible in the world.","Continuity:","Cultists replace people and authority.","The City becomes a target.","The outcome is not merely narrated.","Connected threads: Doll, Cult, Kingdom"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · End Church · Ending branch","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-standing","title":"The Kingdom Left Standing","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Cult can be destroyed while the Kingdom remains broadly unchanged.","Story purpose: Ends one danger without pretending every injustice is solved.","Continuity:","The King still rules.","The political structure remains.","Victory is incomplete.","Connected threads: Kingdom, Cult"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Act I · End Church · Ending branch","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-road","title":"Road to Civilization","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A major trade road continues toward a larger civilized world the player cannot yet enter.","Story purpose: Proves the Kingdom is not the only human center without implying empty space beyond the map.","Continuity:","Merchants use the road.","The destination is visible but inaccessible.","Civilization continues outside the playable realm.","Connected threads: Chapter II, Kingdom"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Chapter II · Chapter II boundary","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-crossroads","title":"The Crossroads Church","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A great Gothic church dominates a fork into the supernatural frontier.","Story purpose: Orients Chapter II through a physical split between distinct routes.","Continuity:","It is separate from Forest Church.","One road leads toward Farm Village.","Others lead toward Pygmy and Troll territories.","Connected threads: Chapter II, Crossroads"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["cathedral","lore"],"notes":["Chapter II · Chapter II gateway","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-farm","title":"Farm Village & Necropolis","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Working farmland gives way immediately to an enormous city of the dead and werewolf hunting ground.","Story purpose: Repeats the link between mass death and supernatural activity at a larger scale.","Continuity:","The farm is the final buffer.","Werewolves occupy the region beyond.","Safety is temporary.","Connected threads: Chapter II, Werewolves"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Chapter II · Chapter II region","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-pygmies","title":"The Pygmy Settlements","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Pygmies possess settlements, culture, interests, knowledge, and quests.","Story purpose: Treats them as a people rather than generic enemies.","Continuity:","A smaller settlement lies in a mountain crevasse.","Isolation preserves forgotten stories.","They need not care about human wars.","Connected threads: Chapter II, Pygmies"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Chapter II · Chapter II people","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-trolls","title":"Mountain Troll Territory","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Beyond the Crossroads, Trolls occupy their own mountain territory and quest network.","Story purpose: Opens a distinct frontier society unrelated to the Hidden Village ascent.","Continuity:","This is Chapter II geography.","It is not the Holy Relief mountain dungeon.","The route continues toward snow and a later locked dungeon.","Connected threads: Chapter II, Trolls"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Chapter II · Chapter II people","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-bridge","title":"The Bridge Troll","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["A sarcastic, deliberately unhelpful Troll comments whenever the player crosses his landmark bridge.","Story purpose: Creates a persistent optional relationship whose removal permanently changes the route.","Continuity:","He is not initially hostile.","He is an extremely dangerous optional fight.","Killing him yields gear but leaves the bridge quiet.","Connected threads: Chapter II, Trolls"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Chapter II · Recurring character","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-snow","title":"The Snow Region","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The frontier mountains rise into snow as familiar borders fall farther behind.","Story purpose: Marks the transition deeper into the wider supernatural world.","Continuity:","It follows Chapter II mountain routes.","The mountain dungeon opens after later progression.","Ordinary civilization recedes.","Connected threads: Chapter II, Snow"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["lore"],"notes":["Chapter II · Chapter II frontier","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-changelings","title":"The Changeling Frontier","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The early Changeling thread expands into the broader nonhuman frontier.","Story purpose: Challenges the belief that Kingdom politics define the whole world.","Continuity:","They are not Cultists.","They are not ordinary forest animals.","Their territory continues beyond early encounters.","Connected threads: Chapter II, Changelings"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","lore"],"notes":["Chapter II · Chapter II continuation","September 19, 2026 · published version 2","Historical narrative reference; chronology and outcome overrides are listed in the merge review."]},{"id":"story-regions","title":"Connected territories","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Start Region — Opening territory: Torture Dungeon · Start Village · Start House · Ossuary","The Forest — Changing wilderness: Forest Church · Wendigo Cave · Changelings · Abandoned Village · Minotaur · Demon Goat Man","Hidden Village — Holy inheritance: Village mountains · Holy Relief dungeon · Old Man’s family","The Kingdom — Human power: Upper City · Lower City · Palace · Prison · Sewers · Opera Hall","Cult Territory — Forbidden Communion: Cult Village · Forgotten Echoes · Dark Dungeon · Dark Relief","Witch / Nun Region — Plague & religion: Swamps · Plague doctors · Gothic Cathedral · Gothic Corridor","The Cult Arena — Ritual spectacle: Empty Colosseum · Nun’s memory · Six sequential battles","The Final Return — Endgame route: Ossuary return · End Church · Demon Father","Chapter II Frontier — Beyond the Crossroads: Farm & Necropolis · Werewolves · Pygmy settlements · Mountain Troll territory · Bridge Troll · Snow · Changelings"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","opening","cathedral","lore"],"notes":[]},{"id":"story-characters","title":"Character motives and transformations","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["The Player: A survivor without memory who inherits the forces that damaged, protected, and seduced everyone before them. Survival → Communion → faction choice → what survives","The Doll: Dark Communion contained until it developed memory and will. It helps whenever help creates more bloodshed. Vessel → waypoints → Priest → Cult → darker path","The Nun: A healer shaped by plague, stranded between life and death, revealed through memories, consumed by final purpose. Healer → threshold → mutations → Six → sacrifice","The Priest: A believer who mistakes a real supernatural mechanism for proof that murder is divine salvation. Faith → shoreline Relief → doctrine → village → Nun","The Old Man: A practitioner who sees his wife’s death as proof that power should be abandoned. Holy magic → accidental harm → grief → withdrawal","The Mage: A son who sees the same tragedy as proof that power must be mastered completely. Hidden Village → Blood → Wendigo → royal protector","The King: A once-liked ruler whose fear creates the army, taxation, and permanent control meant to protect people. Protection → militarization → martial law → possible alliance","The Cult: Heirs to incomplete knowledge who turn reliable bloodshed into worship, society, and spectacle. Fragments → village → Arena → collapse or victory","The Hidden Village: Descendants of those who created the Doll; burdened by guilt and uniquely equipped to resist it. Three Communions → containment → secrecy → resistance"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["travel","cathedral","lore"],"notes":[]},{"id":"story-lore","title":"Lore and rules","source":"storyboard","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms Storyboard","category":"Storyboard","paragraphs":["Death, grief, bone and memory thin the damaged Veil. Ossuaries, churches, plague sites, arenas, graveyards and the Necropolis connect to this premise.","Holy, Blood and Dark are three approaches to the same wound. A Relief is the place where Communion occurs and a spell name is written.","Karma concerns moral action. Dark Points concern Dark Communion. Personality, individual relationships and faction reputation remain separate.","The older story treats the Binding, the Six, the Other Survivor’s death, mutations and the King’s army as history the player cannot simply erase."],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["ending","personality","cathedral","lore"],"notes":[]},{"id":"atlas-story","title":"Main story & choices","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["A shared journey with personal memories. Dialogue choices shape the player; the committed ending changes the campaign.","Design intent: Keep personal reactions and one-time rewards separate from shared progression. The End Church choice decides the finale; the legacy Karma-threshold ending is not part of this route.","How it works:","Meet the Doll → leave the cage → witness the attic memory.","Reach the village → speak with the Barmaid and Priest → choose a pledge, if desired.","Survive the six-demon ordeal. Q05 can begin without the Priest.","Return to the ossuary → confront the ritual at the End Church.","Commit the good or evil route → defeat the Demon Father or the four gate defenders.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Inspect the existing open-world placements before authoring: the original wiring checklist was completed on October 3.","Edit story sources in Docs/Authoring/Story. Dialogue imports update by node ID; quest generation is create-only. Review existing quest assets before changing them.","For added story NPC placements, apply Actor Tag StoryNPC and configure Eclipsed Story > Routes. Keep travel-station dolls untagged.","Connect area overlaps through Eclipsed Story Event Trigger; connect sequence finish AND skip through a Story Sequence Hook.","Use once keys for rewards, player flags for knowledge and world flags for shared progression.","Play both endings, skip cinematics, save/reload and check a host plus guest.","Owner: StoryFlags on PlayerState; Narrative quests; campaign World Events","Network: Server writes progression. Host commits the shared ending; a guest proposes it.","Save behavior: Personal flags and once keys in player records; world flags in the campaign.","Recorded evidence: Oct 8: new-game story world 71 passed / 0 failed. Earlier story report includes explicit forced test steps; this is recorded evidence, not a new run.","Known limits:","The initial “nothing placed” statement in the first-pass report is superseded by its §6 / §9 and the session-h world integration.","Do not reconnect preserved legacy Karma-based ending events to the new route.","Documented command (not executed): run_story_world.ps1 -Only 'tools,run,verify,evil,nopriest,mp'","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Story_FirstPass_2026-10-03.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02h.md","Related guides: arena, jester, social, layers, coop"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · World integrated","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-jester","title":"Jester performances","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Replay a story you have already lived, then return with your campaign restored.","Design intent: Let players revisit completed or failed quests without keeping performance gains or losses. Co-op isolation preserves what the other players do outside the performance.","How it works:","The player opens the nearby stage’s playbill. Only completed or failed quests are eligible.","The replay definition restarts the quest and sets its curtain-up flags, destination layers and cast.","Play the actual story beats. Saving is paused while the performance runs.","Success, failure, death or Leave Performance ends it.","Solo restores the campaign checkpoint; co-op restores the performer while other players keep their progress.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Inspect Story_OperaHall_JesterStage and /Game/Story/Jester/DA_Replay_*; 16 definitions are already covered.","For a new replay, create EclipsedReplayDefinition: Quest, Replayable, Playbill Title / Description, Start From State and Start Transform.","Author CurtainClear/SetPlayerFlags, CurtainClear/SetWorldFlags and CompanionQuests to establish the intended starting beat.","Put required NPCs and props in Performance Cast. Use OnlyIfAbsentWithin for stand-ins, and bHostileOnRelease where needed.","Treat any definition touching shared world flags as alone-only. Wire Eclipsed: Open Jester Playbill into the Jester dialogue.","Test eligibility before granting history; finish, leave and die; compare canonical state after every restore.","Owner: UEclipsedJesterReplaySubsystem; ReplayDefinition; JesterStage","Network: One co-op performer at a time. Shared-world curtain changes are refused in co-op.","Save behavior: Solo verified checkpoint + crash marker; performer-scoped co-op restore. No performance rewards persist.","Recorded evidence: Oct 8: all 16 final performance runs green; each restore compared 31 canonical values. CH01’s real walk remains a separate failure.","Known limits:","CH01 used a TEST SETUP arrival stand-in; the later real-route test was 21 passed / 1 failed.","Earlier “co-op refused” and “no quests enabled” notes are superseded.","Documented command (not executed): run_jester_perform.ps1","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_JesterPerformances.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02g.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01e.md","Related guides: story, travel, layers, coop, changeling"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · 16 performances","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-dolls","title":"Cursed Doll network","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Bind a regional doll by using it, enter training, then choose a bound doll on the world map.","Design intent: Discovery and travel permission are different. Discovering a region reveals its doll; using that doll to enter the arena binds it to that player.","How it works:","Regional dialogue fires NE_ER_TravelToTrainingArena and registers the source doll.","The player arrives at the Arena Doll after the travel transition.","NE_ER_OpenCursedDollTravelMap opens Narrative’s map for that player.","Bound dolls are selectable; discovered but unbound dolls are dimmed.","The server checks the player’s location and binding before travel.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Inspect existing stations first; the manuals document a test-map foundation, not a complete regional placement inventory.","For a new regional doll, place Eclipsed Cursed Doll Station beside it. Set unique Doll Id, Regional role, Associated POI and Training Profile.","Position Arrival P1, Arrival P2 and Arrival Emergency; put the Safety Floor just beneath them.","Apply Cursed Doll Icon To POI, then run Map Check / Data Validation.","Place or inspect the TrainingArena-role station with DL_TrainingArena.","Wire regional dialogue to NE_ER_TravelToTrainingArena; Arena dialogue to NE_ER_OpenCursedDollTravelMap and optionally NE_ER_ReturnFromTrainingArena.","Test bound/unbound choices, cancel, save/restore and separate-player travel; manually test mouse selection.","Owner: AEclipsedCursedDollStation; UEclipsedCursedDoll subsystem","Network: Per-player map and travel. Server validates each destination.","Save behavior: Bindings per player. Loading an arena save returns to the source doll.","Recorded evidence: Session h: Doll / Training / fog-exclusion route 39/0. Session g: solo, couch and remote-client doll-map proofs.","Known limits:","Mouse doll-marker selection was not automated in session g.","Session-f “world map not built” is superseded by session g.","Documented command (not executed): run_doll_proof.ps1 -Mode run","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02g.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01f.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02h.md","Related guides: training, travel, maps, coop"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Test-proven system","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-training","title":"Training arena","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Fight copies of real enemies, gain normal XP, and leave the world’s history untouched.","Design intent: Training uses production stats, equipment, abilities and AI, but excludes loot, crime, karma, persistent world memory and quest kill credit.","How it works:","The source doll selects the regional Training Profile.","Hold Interact for one second on Start Training.","The director spawns training copies and tracks their summons.","Kills grant XP; other world consequences and loot are excluded.","All participants down or the last player leaving resets only the run’s actors.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Open /Game/Maps/DevMaps/L_EclipsedCursedDollTest to inspect the working fixture.","In DL_TrainingArena, place Eclipsed Training Start Point beside the Arena Doll.","Set the Arena station’s Enemy Spawn Points and Arena Respawn Delay (documented default: 3 seconds).","Duplicate DA_ER_Training_CultVillage for a new region; list every real NPC definition needed and assign the profile to its station.","Optionally wire NE_ER_StartTraining into the Arena Doll dialogue.","Verify XP is granted but loot, karma, crimes and quest kills are not; die, leave, and save/reload.","Owner: EclipsedTrainingRun director and profile assets","Network: Arena presentation is per view / per machine. Online clients prepare copies from listed profiles.","Save behavior: Training enemies are not restored. Loading returns the player to the source doll.","Recorded evidence: Session g: training run 23/0; fresh restore 2/0 + 2/0. Packaged Development run 23/0.","Known limits:","The session-f “director not built” / “tag unread” notes are superseded by session g.","Documented command (not executed): run_training_proof.ps1 -Mode run","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02g.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02g.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02h.md","Related guides: dolls, combat, social, coop"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Test-proven system","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-social","title":"Witnesses & consequences","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["NPC individuals remember what they actually witnessed. One attack event creates one updating consequence card.","Design intent: Keep crime evidence, personal memory and player-facing feedback consistent. Two guards of one definition remain two distinct witnesses.","How it works:","An attack creates incidents grouped by player and damage source.","Eligible individual witnesses record the event according to awareness rules.","Karma / faction effects follow incident rules; newly hostile NPCs are identified.","One card updates in place as later witnesses are confirmed.","Remembered incidents inform later conversations and may reach law enforcement.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Tune Project Settings > Game > Eclipsed Consequences: AssaultGroupingSeconds (3 seconds) and FeedEntrySeconds (12 seconds).","Author social identities and ties through NPC definitions and the awareness Ties asset.","Keep per-instance witness identity intact; do not regenerate production NPC IDs to solve card counts.","Attack near two same-definition guards, repeat a hit and introduce a late witness. Check one updated card with distinct remembered individuals.","Save and reload, then test the second couch player’s separate card and memory.","Owner: ConsequenceSubsystem; AwarenessSubsystem; SocialStateComponent","Network: Server decides; each player’s SocialView feeds their own HUD.","Save behavior: Incident / knowledge records and social relationships persist under stable player save identity.","Recorded evidence: Session h: guards 24/0; consequence rules 38/0 + 5/0; packaged guards 24/0.","Known limits:","Oct 8 notes a pre-existing guards-proof regression; do not treat the earlier green test as current regression clearance.","Documented command (not executed): run_guards.ps1 -Tag atlas","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01e.md","Related guides: responses, law, coop, training"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Runtime proven","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-responses","title":"NPC voices & reactions","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Give guards, villagers, knights and thieves distinct responses without changing their factions.","Design intent: Reusable response categories provide direct-hit, witnessed-assault and remembered-assault lines, with variation between nearby speakers.","How it works:","Assign a Response Category explicitly or match a rule by definition.","The server selects a variant for the situation and keeps its context.","Nearby speakers avoid the same variant; an NPC avoids its previous one.","Spoken lines use Narrative’s dialogue position, queue during conversations and avoid duplicates.","Remembered-assault dialogue offers apology, self-defence claim, threat or leave.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Edit Docs/Authoring/Responses/Categories/<Category>.json and the corresponding Dialogues JSON.","Run EclipsedTools.ImportResponseCategories from Session Frontend > Automation.","Assign NPC Definition > Social > Dialogue > Response Category, or add a category rule under Eclipsed NPC Responses.","Use CharacterIds / DefinitionNameContains and Priority to control matching.","Test two adjacent guards and a villager, then revisit remembered conversations and check simultaneous subtitle spacing.","Owner: UEclipsedResponseCategory; SocialModules; SocialNotices","Network: Server selects the line; clients display the result.","Save behavior: Persistent memories come from consequences; categories are authored data.","Recorded evidence: Session h: responses 24/0 in editor and package.","Known limits:","Categories are not factions. An uncategorized NPC retains its existing behavior.","Documented command (not executed): run_tool.ps1 -Test EclipsedTools.ImportResponseCategories","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02h.md","Related guides: social, law, story"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Runtime proven","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-law","title":"Kingdom law & custody","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["A witnessed or reported illegal act can lead to confrontation, bribery, arrest and custody.","Design intent: Law consumes existing evidence; it does not invent witnesses. Jurisdiction policy defines arrestable actions and server-owned cases drive the response.","How it works:","An identified enforcer witnesses a crime, or receives a report.","The Kingdom policy judges the act and the law subsystem opens a response.","Dialogue offers applicable accept, refuse and bribe outcomes.","Custody uses jail cells and a belongings chest; protected quest items stay with the player.","Standing, custody and belongings persist in the player’s own law record.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Inspect Project Settings > Eclipsed Law: open-world enablement, jurisdictions, enforcers and royals.","Inspect existing Kingdom_Cell2 / 3 / 5 / 6 and Kingdom_BelongingsChest in the city dungeon.","After moving the dungeon, rerun EclipsedTools.Law.KingdomCells. For new cells, set unique CellId, Jurisdiction, door width, escort acceptance and interior layers; local +X points out.","Author confrontation in Docs/Authoring/Law/Law_Confrontation.json; use NC_ER_LawCanBribe and NE_ER_LawAccept/Refuse/Pay.","Protect required quest items with Eclipsed.Item.KeepOnArrest or KeepOnArrestClasses.","Test arrest, bribe, refusal, reinforcement, persistence and a remote client before extending a jurisdiction.","Owner: LawSubsystem (cases); LawRecord on PlayerState; JailCell / BelongingsChest","Network: Server authority; player law record replicates owner-only.","Save behavior: Offenses, payoffs, royal status, custody and belongings in the player record.","Recorded evidence: Dedicated fixture, persistence, multiplayer and live-dungeon proof runners are documented. Consult the law ledger for authoritative row statuses.","Known limits:","First dungeon relocation measured about 40 seconds of dark screen.","Two local gamepads, four players, real palace royals and crash during custody transfer remain unproven.","Documented command (not executed): run_law_suite.ps1","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_KingdomLaw.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md","Related guides: social, responses, layers, coop"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · World enabled","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-combat","title":"Combat & weapon techniques","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Weapon techniques, contact timing, facing and shared combat rules make player and NPC attacks readable.","Design intent: A strike should contact the target in its path, without stale melee-warp targets or reward rules bypassing the normal damage pipeline.","How it works:","Input or NPC selection activates the technique ability.","Each strike clears stale melee warp targets and plays its montage / travel.","StrikeContactTask watches the path and stops travel at contact.","HitTime applies damage through Narrative’s damage execution and the shared crit rule.","Impact cues and the lock-on health trail communicate the result.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Inspect the weapon’s UEclipsedWeaponTechnique data asset and Project Settings > Eclipsed Weapon Techniques.","Use the Devkit / Combat Arena to compare a known technique before changing timings or travel.","For NPCs, check equipment eligibility and the definition’s technique configuration; a bowless archer must fall back to usable equipment.","Test a strike after respawn, a leap toward a target and an opponent moving through the wind-up.","Review standing versus moving Dodge: Q activates the stock GA_Dodge only while moving.","Manually review bow-aim camera and overlapping G / D-pad Right bindings before deciding changes.","Owner: WeaponTechniqueAbility; StrikeContactTask; NPCTechniques; Narrative GAS damage","Network: Player ability runs on server + owning client; NPC attacks are server-driven.","Save behavior: Player technique state via Narrative savable component.","Recorded evidence: Session f: facing and contact fixes proven. Oct 8: input proof 9/0 and lock-panel tiers 5/0 each.","Known limits:","G still means Throw + Summon Board; D-pad Right still means Quick Use + Map. User decision remains.","Torch Sweep has no burn while its strength is unset.","Bow aim (R63 / E-037) and feel/visual items still need user review.","Documented command (not executed): Eclipsed.ArenaDev 1","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-01f.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01e.md, EclipsedRealms_Architecture_Map_2026-10-01e.md, EclipsedRealms_NPC_Weapon_Techniques.md","Related guides: creatures, relief, devkit, coop"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Implemented + proofs","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-relief","title":"Relief magic & player HUD","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Carried Reliefs govern magic access, with readable refusals and per-player presentation.","Design intent: An NPC needs the carried Relief for its school’s magic. Player UI reads authoritative attributes and surfaces why a cast was refused.","How it works:","The character equips or carries the applicable Relief and meets the ability requirements.","The spell uses its existing ability rules; a refusal reaches the player.","The spell presents its school’s effects, including Dark Curse, Void Pulse and Void Stasis.","HUD and player information read current state; the empty dock hides over loading and menus.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Read the Relief Kit guide for the school and its spell requirements before assigning a loadout.","For NPC magic, verify the carried Relief, selected school and the existing NPC magic configuration.","Use the Relief proof map to cast each assigned spell and test refusal cases.","For Dark, compare Curse, Void Pulse and Void Stasis presentation; check the dock during loading and menus.","Check the owning player’s HUD in solo, couch and a remote-client session.","Owner: ReliefKitSpells; ReliefKitHUD; PlayerInfo tabs; GAS attributes","Network: Gameplay authority remains in the existing ability systems; UI belongs to the local player.","Save behavior: Underlying character / ability state, not duplicated UI calculations.","Recorded evidence: Session f: Dark 128/0, Stasis 101/0; Oct 8 travel regression includes the dock visibility fix.","Known limits:","Spell and balance specifics are in the bundled Relief guides; the atlas does not infer new tuning.","Documented command (not executed): run_kit.ps1 -School Dark","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-01f.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01f.md, EclipsedRealms_Relief_Kit.md, NPC_Relief_Magic_AI.md","Related guides: combat, training, coop, travel"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Implemented + proofs","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-creatures","title":"NPCs, creatures & spawning","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Keep definition data, appearance, attack sets and spawn lifecycle aligned.","Design intent: Narrative owns NPC lifecycle. Project systems extend creature attacks, appearance validation and safe spawning while preserving that ownership.","How it works:","A definition supplies identity, appearance, equipment, tiers and attack configuration.","Narrative’s spawner creates the NPC; the project spawner adds temporary ground support.","CreatureAttackAbility uses the definition’s attack set, with cues on every machine.","Narrative owns respawn, tether, removal, save and streaming lifecycle.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Create from a compatible NPC template in the Devkit; check unique definition identity and body / clothing family.","Assign CreatureAttacks and an appropriate ability configuration for non-humanoids.","For new placements, put Eclipsed NPC Spawner on the ground and add NPC Spawn Component > NPC To Spawn.","Inspect Spawn Support: default Z offset 150 cm and support half extent 75 × 75 × 5 cm.","Check Boss / Elite DefaultOwnedTags and verify the lock-on panel tier.","Test attacks, save/load, and streaming out/back in; inspect zoo-map creature notes for the bat and Wendigo specifics.","Owner: Narrative NPC definitions / spawn components; EclipsedNPCSpawner; CreatureAttackAbility","Network: Spawning and hits on server; creature presentation cues on clients.","Save behavior: Narrative’s lifecycle. Support components unload with the spawner.","Recorded evidence: Session f creature attacks proven; packaged spawner tests 6/0, 4/0, 10/0. Oct 8 tier assignment and bar checks recorded.","Known limits:","Existing spawners are unchanged; the new class is for new placements.","Documented command (not executed): -EclipsedSpawnerProof","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01e.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-01f.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md","Related guides: combat, social, layers, devkit"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Implemented + proofs","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-horses","title":"Horses & NPC riding","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Players and NPCs mount through Narrative interaction; riding orders coordinate NPC travel.","Design intent: Keep riders seated consistently across the network, prevent weapon use while mounted, and make dismounting a controlled stop.","How it works:","Interact with a horse; weapons are put away before mounting.","The rider controls movement or follows an NPC Ride To order.","Remote players and late joiners see the rider attached at saddle height.","Hold Interact to brake and then dismount.","An NPC returns to its normal AI after the order finishes or is cancelled.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Use an existing NPC_Horse / BP_EclipsedHorse; no new player-mount actor is required.","For an NPC route, call the latent Blueprint node Eclipsed NPC Ride To with NPC, Mount and Destination.","Handle Arrived / Failed or the Ride Order On Finished result; handle competing claims and cancellations.","Ride, gallop, steer and hold Interact to dismount; test with a remote rider and a late joiner.","Test couch player 2 leaving while mounted and verify the horse remains.","Owner: HorseLocomotion; MountRider; NPCRiding; RideOrder","Network: Server decides mount / dismount and claims. Remote attachment and animation are synchronized.","Save behavior: Uses existing character / mount lifecycle; inspect current manual for tested restore paths.","Recorded evidence: Session f: horse MP 36/0 twice, horse rules 27/0, NPC riding SP and MP. Session h adds turning / couch camera work.","Known limits:","Physical controllers still need hands-on verification.","Session-g note: post-leave horse controller was not compared with normal dismount.","Documented command (not executed): run_horse_mp.ps1 -Tag atlas","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01f.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-01f.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02g.md","Related guides: coop, travel, maps"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Runtime proven","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-maps","title":"Maps & exploration","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Exploration belongs to each player, with separate fog, markers and map interaction.","Design intent: Reveal places a player has actually explored. A revealed destination does not imply a discovered travel route or a bound doll.","How it works:","Exploration samples the player’s position at the configured cadence.","The player’s mask reveals nearby cells; teleport reveals the arrival only.","Each local view draws its own fog texture and markers.","World-map controls select or inspect markers; doll mode applies additional binding rules.","Packed exploration state restores from the player’s own save.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Inspect Project Settings for Map Exploration and the map’s MapTileBounds before tuning cell coverage.","Test wheel zoom, hover, double-click selection and drag pan on the world map.","Test gamepad pan, reticle hover, confirm and Back.","Move two couch players apart and verify each minimap clears only its own area.","Save, close the process and reload both players; check training and Jester do not reveal canonical exploration.","Owner: MapExploration; MapMarkers; Narrative world map","Network: Per-player state and unique texture per local view.","Save behavior: Packed exploration in player records, with compatibility for the earlier format.","Recorded evidence: Session h: open-world map 23/0; couch 8/0 + 6/0; kit maps 51/0.","Known limits:","Physical controller input was simulated in the proofs.","Doll-mode mouse selection needs its separate manual check.","Documented command (not executed): run_fog.ps1 -Mode world -Map /Game/Maps/L_EclipsedRealms_OpenWorldMap -TimeoutSec 900","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02g.md","Related guides: dolls, travel, coop, jester"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Runtime proven","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-travel","title":"Travel & arrival","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Move the traveller, bring the camera with them, and return control after the destination loads.","Design intent: A travel is complete only when the pawn, camera, world loading and presentation agree about the arrival.","How it works:","A destination / transform travel starts for the affected player.","Loading presentation covers relocation and streaming.","Ragdoll ends before arrival teleport.","The camera snaps to the arrived pawn so streaming follows the destination.","Presentation closes, appropriate pause state clears and TravelFinished fires.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Use the shared TravelSubsystem route when adding transform travel, rather than independent fixed-coordinate teleports.","Provide safe arrival transforms and ground support for stations.","Check the camera, pawn position, paused state and Relief dock after each transition.","Test death / ragdoll before travel and a remote guest’s arrival.","Use separate -UserDir profiles for loopback host and guest so campaign admission does not see duplicate identities.","Owner: TravelSubsystem; TravelTransitionComponent; camera owner integration","Network: Traveller-specific presentation; camera correction also runs later for remote clients.","Save behavior: Destination systems decide return / save policy; travel itself is the shared transition.","Recorded evidence: Oct 8: solo 56/0, remote host 19/0 and client 9/0.","Known limits:","First dungeon relocation can show a dark screen for about 40 seconds.","V4 packaged finisher → death → respawn → camera smoke remains pending.","Documented command (not executed): run_travel.ps1 -MP","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md, EclipsedRealms_JesterPerformances.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-01f.md","Related guides: dolls, jester, horses, layers, coop"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Runtime proven","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-layers","title":"Interiors & data layers","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Doors, quests, law and performances hold interiors loaded until everyone is finished with them.","Design intent: One door closing must not unload an interior another player, door or story system still needs.","How it works:","A door or gameplay system requests the interior’s runtime data layers.","Named holders keep shared ownership while content is needed.","Opening waits for interior readiness where configured.","Closing unloads only when players are outside and no other holder needs the layers.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","For a new doorway, place BP_EP_DataLayerDoor and orient its arrow toward the outside.","Set Interior Data Layers, Unload Interior On Close, Wait For Interior Before Opening and its timeout.","Set Open Yaw, Swing Duration / Curve and interaction text.","Use Eclipsed: Hold Data Layers / Release Data Layers for independent quest or cinematic needs.","Test two doors, two players and save/load; inspect the ownership dump if content vanishes early.","Owner: DataLayerDoor; DataLayerOwnershipSubsystem","Network: Server authority and reference-counted ownership.","Save behavior: Door / world state uses the campaign; runtime holders belong to their owning systems.","Recorded evidence: Session e: seven door / ownership tests passed in isolation. Oct 8: Jester destination layers now use a named holder.","Known limits:","Do not bulk-replace existing doors or target DL_World. The documents do not claim a complete door migration.","Documented command (not executed): Eclipsed.DataLayers.DumpOwnership","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01e.md, EclipsedRealms_JesterPerformances.md, EclipsedRealms_KingdomLaw.md","Related guides: travel, story, law, jester, creatures"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Shared ownership","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-coop","title":"Co-op, identity & saves","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Share the world while keeping each player’s character, knowledge, UI and saved progress distinct.","Design intent: Stable save identity must survive display-name changes, campaign loads and reconnects. Couch players get their own input, menus and records.","How it works:","Online guests join the host; a second local pad presses Start on a gameplay map.","Each player gets an owning view, UI and stable identity; LocalP2 is scoped to the campaign slot.","Save writes the world and player records; the selected slot becomes the active campaign.","Host Load restores listening; online guests reconnect after the map change.","Couch player 2 pauses and holds View / Back for 1.5 seconds to save and leave.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Connect two physical controllers and start a gameplay map. Pad 2 Start joins; keyboard / mouse and pad 1 remain player 1.","Open each player’s menu and verify input never moves the other player’s focus.","Leave with pad 2 Start then hold View / Back; rejoin and verify character and inventory.","Save from the pause menu, close and reload; verify standalone player-2 persistence.","Host online, join with a different profile, change campaign slot, load and reconnect.","For a new guest appearance, use Create Character + Join in the multiplayer menu; cancel should cancel the join.","Owner: CouchCoop; SaveSubsystem; HostContinuity; SplitScreenScaler","Network: Only the host machine can add a couch player; maximum two local players.","Save behavior: One file per player. Standalone couch persistence is fixed in session h.","Recorded evidence: Session g packaged couch 75/0; Shipping smoke 13/0. Session h confirms fresh-process standalone P2 restore.","Known limits:","Physical pads remain untested; automated input was injected at Slate entry points.","Unplugging pad 2 mid-game is not handled in the session-g handoff.","The older “use ?listen for P2 saves” limitation is superseded.","Documented command (not executed): run_coop_persist.ps1","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02g.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02g.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md","Related guides: story, jester, maps, horses, law"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Packaged proofs","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-arena","title":"Demon Arena & Nun ritual","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["A staged six-demon encounter owns containment, spectacle, progression and resumable completion.","Design intent: One demon at a time, one counted death per stage, and a world completion state that survives a reload.","How it works:","Enter the arena; the linked Nun encounter can trigger the opening.","The director locks doors, enables containment, reveals the crowd and starts storm events.","Each stage summons a demon; actual defeated stages advance the shared objective.","Six defeats complete Q05 and begin the next story beat.","Saved progress resumes at the next demon; a completed encounter does not restart.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Inspect the existing world director and the Nun link before adding a duplicate.","For a new director, set Encounter Tag, six Stages, Spawn Transforms and the optional Nun Encounter.","Configure Doors To Lock and Containment Actors at every escapable boundary.","Assign spectators, summon effects / sounds and start / end weather events.","Connect Stage Defeated Events and Completion Events to the intended quest route.","Test interruption at 4/6, fresh-process resume, duplicate deaths and completion; verify Jester replay resets the encounter state.","Owner: AEclipsedDemonArenaDirector; NunStoryEncounter; Narrative quest events","Network: Shared encounter and objective; trigger should be inside containment.","Save behavior: Defeated count is a world fact; completion is the encounter’s World Event tag.","Recorded evidence: Session f map proof 18/0 + 7/0. Oct 8 Q04H, Q04E and Q05 performances passed.","Known limits:","A player outside the arena when it starts stays outside; place the trigger deliberately.","Early manuals’ “not placed” status is superseded by story world integration.","Documented command (not executed): -EclipsedDemonArenaProof=run","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01e.md, EclipsedRealms_Story_FirstPass_2026-10-03.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md, EclipsedRealms_JesterPerformances.md","Related guides: story, jester, combat, layers"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · World integrated","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-changeling","title":"Changeling & Hidden Village","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Two side-story chains connect the household mystery, the Jester, and the Hidden Village’s trust and hunt.","Design intent: Use authored quests and real story interactions. Separate a successful staged proof from a route the player and escort can actually walk.","How it works:","CH01: meet the boy in the woods and escort him home.","CH02: meet the mother, attend dinner, see the reveal and survive the household.","CH03: clear the passage / Wendigo and reach the theatre’s Jester.","HV01–02: meet the Old Man, hunt one of each listed animal, report and receive teaching.","HV03: visit the palace Mage, hear the refusal and bring the answer home.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Inspect Docs/Authoring/Changeling and Docs/Authoring/HiddenVillage for quest and dialogue sources.","Walk CH01 from the woods to the actual house door with the boy; do not substitute a test arrival.","Decide a slope / collision correction for the hollow at (14825, -38340, -747), then rebuild navigation and repeat the route.","Review the dinner reveal face camera and the still-visible HUD / interaction prompt.","Test hunt credit, trust progression and the palace interior in normal play and eligible Jester performances.","Owner: ChangelingHousehold; HiddenVillage; Narrative quests and story actors","Network: Performance isolation applies; household replays are alone-only, Hidden Village replays are co-op eligible.","Save behavior: Uses story player records, world flags and Narrative quest progress.","Recorded evidence: Oct 8: dinner 14/0; face frame examined. Real CH01 route 21/1; the boy followed about 110 m before the hollow blocked arrival.","Known limits:","Navigation currently claims a slope the characters cannot climb. The hollow trapped both for 270 seconds.","Navmesh builder was stopped early in empty outer space.","Documented command (not executed): run_jester_perform.ps1","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md, EclipsedRealms_JesterPerformances.md","Related guides: story, jester, layers"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Route issue remains","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-devkit","title":"Authoring & validation tools","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Create data safely, inspect fights, and use focused proofs before attempting a complete package.","Design intent: Authoring tools create content; gameplay remains owned by runtime systems. Test helpers and fixtures are not evidence of an unassisted player journey.","How it works:","Choose the system and its existing asset / template.","Author in the Devkit, data assets or documented source scripts.","Validate identity, references and configuration.","Run a focused isolated-map proof, then the real-world path.","Use package tests when authorized and keep product Shipping separate from the smoke target.","Authoring and review notes (historical documentation):","Open the Eclipsed Realms Devkit and inspect its staged NPC Database create / delete workflow.","Use matching source formats and documented import tools; preserve hand-authored content and follow create-only quest semantics.","For hands-on combat, open L_EclipsedCombatArenas and Eclipsed.ArenaDev 1; choose teams / equipment, Spawn, then Start.","Keep proof profiles isolated with -UserDir; record simulated input and setup bypasses explicitly.","Treat V4 packaging as pending the user’s explicit instruction; prepare a finisher → death → respawn → camera smoke checklist.","For a product build, use EclipsedRealms, never the EclipsedRealmsSmoke test target.","Owner: Editor Devkit; NarrativeAuthoring; Dev proof subsystems","Network: Test the relevant solo, couch and remote-client paths independently.","Save behavior: Isolated proof profiles / throwaway slots; authoring data is source content.","Recorded evidence: Handoffs document editor, Development package and separate Shipping smoke results. Latest Oct 8 build 8263 has no new package.","Known limits:","This atlas displays handoff evidence; it has not run Unreal, revalidated gameplay or executed any game commands.","Documented command (not executed): Eclipsed.ArenaDev 1","Source document names: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-01e.md, EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02h.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-02g.md, EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md","Related guides: combat, creatures, story, coop"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Snapshot through October 8, 2026 · Editor tooling","Evidence is dated; this consolidation does not rerun gameplay tests."]},{"id":"atlas-priority-nav","title":"Resolve the Changeling route","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Choose the slope / collision fix for the south-east hollow, rebuild navigation, then walk the boy all the way to the house door. The staged arrival is not a pass.","Completion criterion: Player and boy reach the real door without intervention.","Source: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":[],"notes":["Historical outstanding work · Decision + repair"]},{"id":"atlas-priority-pads","title":"Run the physical-controller pass","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Use two real pads: join, independent movement / menus, leave, rejoin, mounted leave and Jester exit. Observe pad-2 unplug behavior.","Completion criterion: Record pad models, Steam Input state and actual results.","Source: EclipsedRealms_Usage_Manual_2026-10-02g.md"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":[],"notes":["Historical outstanding work · Hands-on check"]},{"id":"atlas-priority-feel","title":"Make camera and input decisions","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Review bow aim R63 / E-037, moving-only Dodge, G dual binding and D-pad Right dual binding. Include the dinner reveal overlay and the ~40 s dungeon transition.","Completion criterion: Record desired behavior before changing bindings or camera tuning.","Source: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":[],"notes":["Historical outstanding work · User review"]},{"id":"atlas-priority-regression","title":"Recheck the outstanding proofs","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Investigate the guards-proof regression noted Oct 8 and the Arrowstorm review-mode artifact. Check doll-map mouse selection and law’s unproven configurations separately.","Completion criterion: New evidence names the build, path, input method and any bypass.","Source: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":[],"notes":["Historical outstanding work · Validation"]},{"id":"atlas-priority-package","title":"Authorize and validate V4","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["The latest handoff explicitly leaves V4 packaging for the user to request. Include packaged smokes for finisher → death → respawn → camera; run R1 respawn last.","Completion criterion: Authorized package completes and the required packaged playtests are recorded.","Source: EclipsedRealms_Handoff_2026-10-08.md"],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":[],"notes":["Historical outstanding work · Awaiting user instruction"]},{"id":"atlas-playbill","title":"The 16-performance playbill","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Q01 · The One Who Woke · Doll → cage exit → ground floor · Main · Alone","Q02 · What the House Remembers · Attic Doll → unlock → memory · Main · Alone","Q03 · A Village at Prayer · Tavern → gallows → Priest · Main · Alone","Q04H · An End to the Offering · Holy pledge → six-demon ordeal · Good · Alone","Q04E · Worthy of the Offering · Evil pledge → six-demon ordeal · Evil · Alone","Q05 · The Sixfold Ordeal · Nun → six demons → arena exit · Main · Alone","Q06 · Where the Dead Wait · Ossuary → End Church → explicit choice · Main · Alone","Q07H · No More Offerings · Good commitment → Demon Father · Good · Alone","Q07E · Let the Kingdom Answer · Evil commitment → summoning → four defenders · Evil · Alone","CH01 · A Child in the Woods · Boy → escort → daughter greeting · Side · Alone","CH02 · A Place at the Table · Mother → dinner → reveal → ambush · Side · Alone","CH03 · Behind the House · Passage → Wendigo → Jester · Side · Alone","HV01 · What Faith Cannot Teach · Old Man → trial → report → teaching · Side · Co-op eligible","HV02 · One of Each · Moose, goat, cow, bear, deer → report · Side · Co-op eligible","HV03 · A Place Still Kept · Mage → refusal → answer home · Side · Co-op eligible","BearCave · The Wendigo Cave · Existing cave performance · Side · Co-op eligible"],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":[],"notes":["Completed or failed quest eligibility still applies; the listed co-op restrictions are the October 8 snapshot."]},{"id":"atlas-progress-rules","title":"What happens to progress?","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["Training kill, any mode: normal XP; no loot, karma, crime, witness/world memory or quest kill credit. Training copies and summons belong to the run.","Solo Jester performance: restore the verified campaign checkpoint, including XP, items, quests, world flags and canonical state.","Co-op Jester performance: isolate and restore the performer while other players retain their progress. Saving is paused for everyone; replays that change shared world flags are refused.","Online guest ending choice: the guest proposes a route; the host must confirm it at the altar. A proposal does not commit the shared ending.","Host or solo ending choice: commit the route once. Shared quests advance and the deciding player receives the one-time karma consequence.","Load in solo: restore campaign and player records. An arena save returns to its source Doll.","Load as host: reload while retaining hosting; online guests reconnect and restore their own records. Standalone local player two has a saved file.","An early pledge and the final End Church commitment are different decisions. Q05 can begin without the Priest.","The playbill’s alone/co-op labels apply to replays, not normal campaign play. Developer-granted history is not player eligibility. Legacy and test-map quests are not the production replay roster."],"spoiler":true,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["Preserved from the Atlas’s progress explainer and story view; no game simulation or test was executed."]},{"id":"atlas-timeline","title":"How later handoffs changed the plan","source":"atlas","sourceTitle":"Eclipsed Realms · Design Atlas","category":"Project atlas","paragraphs":["October 1 (sessions e/f): techniques, horses, spawners, Jester and Doll foundations; several systems were test-map only.","October 2 (session g): Doll map travel, training rules, isolated Jester co-op and couch join/leave built.","October 3 (session h and addenda): individual witnesses, response categories, fog, standalone couch persistence and story wiring in the real world.","October 8: 16 performances, travel fixes, Kingdom law, tier/input refinements; real CH01 route and V4 package remained pending.","Checklists describe repeatable authoring/review work, not missing features. Recorded passes and completion checks are historical evidence, not a live audit.","System relationships are curated design connections, not a generated code dependency graph. The original checklist contained 106 review steps; browser-local completion marks are not game state."],"spoiler":false,"conflicts":["balance"],"notes":["October 11 Atlas assembly · documentation through October 8."]}],"conflicts":[{"id":"play-modes","topic":"Solo and co-op","kind":"Resolved conflict","older":"Eclipsed Realms describes the game as single-player. Discover describes online and local co-op.","decision":"Keep About: solo, online guests in the host’s world, and up to two local players on the host machine. Do not turn four-player or 2 + 2 targets into confirmed support.","sources":["original","discover"],"terms":["single-player","multiplayer","co-op"]},{"id":"travel","topic":"Discovery versus fast travel","kind":"Resolved conflict","older":"The original promises unlimited travel to discovered waypoints; Discover also offers travel to previously discovered origins.","decision":"Keep About: discovering a region and binding its Cursed Doll are separate. Using a regional Doll to enter training binds that destination to the individual player; the Arena Doll offers bound destinations.","sources":["original","discover","storyboard"],"terms":["waypoint","travel","doll"]},{"id":"ending","topic":"How the campaign ending is chosen","kind":"Resolved conflict","older":"The original frames the outcome around faction allegiance and standing. Older moral-route language can imply that karma selects the ending.","decision":"Keep About: the decisive ending is an explicit story choice, committed by the host. The Design Atlas places it at the End Church and explicitly excludes the legacy karma-threshold route. Faction relationships remain distinct.","sources":["original","discover","storyboard"],"terms":["ending","outcome","karma","kingdom"]},{"id":"opening","topic":"Opening location and attic chronology","kind":"Older sources disagree","older":"The original opens among bodies in the ossuary beneath a house; Storyboard and Discover open in the Torture Dungeon. Storyboard places the attic memory late in Act I.","decision":"Use the project-backed Design Atlas sequence alongside About: Doll → cage exit → attic memory → village. About does not name the exact opening room, so retain its neutral wording. Preserve the older named locations and late-memory ordering as historical story proposals.","sources":["original","discover","storyboard"],"terms":["ossuary","torture","attic","awakening"]},{"id":"magic","topic":"Spell rosters, schools and ultimate slots","kind":"Resolved conflict","older":"The original lists Blood Rain, Area Bleed and Blood Meteor and puts Flesh Demon under Dark. Discover uses the newer Blood list, but advertises five spells plus a separate ultimate and omits Void Stasis.","decision":"Keep About’s named examples, including Blood Offering, Blood Rush, Blood Rupture and Dark Void Stasis. The Atlas’s bundled Relief Kit identifies rank/slot 5 as the ultimate and Summon Demon as Blood. Retain other old names, slot counts and exact tuning only as historical reference, not a complete current spell roster.","sources":["original","discover"],"terms":["relief","spell","magic","blood","dark","ultimate"]},{"id":"casting","topic":"Relief access and release","kind":"Wording narrowed","older":"Discover says the Relief must always be wielded and deployed. The original describes a fixed influence size and fixed controller behavior.","decision":"Keep About’s carry-or-equip wording and ability-specific requirements. Costs commit on release; an interruption before release spends no cost. Do not generalize every old placement, radius or binding rule to every current ability.","sources":["original","discover"],"terms":["relief","spell","casting","controller"]},{"id":"jester","topic":"Jester eligibility and restoration","kind":"Resolved conflict","older":"Discover limits replays to completed main quests and says they award no XP or loot.","decision":"Keep About: eligible completed or failed quests, including side quests, can become performances. Campaign state is restored and gains/losses do not carry back. Some are solo-only; the Atlas supports performer-only restoration in eligible co-op performances.","sources":["discover"],"terms":["jester","performance","replay"]},{"id":"personality","topic":"Personality names","kind":"Needs confirmation","older":"Original and Storyboard use Cruel / Cunning / Compassionate. Discover uses Witty / Empathetic / Bold.","decision":"About supplies no authoritative three-label set. Use general wording about dialogue and relationships on the main page; preserve both sets here until the project confirms the names.","sources":["original","discover","storyboard"],"terms":["personality","cruel","witty","compassionate"]},{"id":"cathedral","topic":"Cathedral, Nun and Witch Priest naming","kind":"Needs confirmation","older":"Original and Storyboard associate the Gothic Cathedral with the Witch/Nun region; Discover also labels the supplied cathedral as Cult territory and uses Witch Priest.","decision":"Keep neutral descriptions of the religious regions. Do not merge distinct churches or declare Witch Priest and Nun interchangeable. Gallery captions retain the supplied cathedral-reference label without confirming the final in-game location.","sources":["original","discover","storyboard"],"terms":["cathedral","witch","nun","church"]},{"id":"targets","topic":"Unvalidated modes and progression promises","kind":"Design targets only","older":"Discover lists four online players, 2 + 2 households, dungeon helpers, 1v1–4v4 arenas and New Game+ / New Game++.","decision":"Preserve as older design targets in the archive. About confirms solo, online guests, two local players, training and conditional replay. It does not establish those extra configurations or modes as available.","sources":["discover"],"terms":["multiplayer","dungeon","competitive","new game","progression"]},{"id":"balance","topic":"Numbers, bindings and feature availability","kind":"Not revalidated","older":"Older pages specify health/damage curves, XP pacing, armor bonuses, starting points, spell tuning, Dark Point penalties, day/night ratios and controller bindings.","decision":"Preserve the dated values for reference; do not import them as current promises. The Atlas also records input conflicts, pending physical-controller checks and a guards-proof regression. Historical test passes do not validate today’s game build.","sources":["original","discover","atlas"],"terms":["combat","character","magic","relief","world","coop","social"]},{"id":"lore","topic":"Lore, endings and Chapter II","kind":"Historical narrative / spoilers","older":"The older sites add the First Binding, character motives, irreversible events, faction outcomes and a Chapter II frontier.","decision":"Merge the shared premise and neutral regional context into About. Preserve all 49 storyboard beats behind a spoiler control. Older detailed outcomes and Chapter II geography remain narrative reference; absence from About is not proof of implementation or a contradiction.","sources":["original","discover","storyboard"],"terms":["story","chapter","binding","doll","nun","survivor","frontier"]},{"id":"demons","topic":"Arena enemy names","kind":"Needs confirmation","older":"Original and Storyboard call the six arena enemies Greater Flesh Demons.","decision":"Keep About/Atlas’s neutral six-demon ordeal language. The Atlas’s bundled session-f record explicitly declines to infer that the six numbered NPC definitions are the Flesh Demon roster. Retain the older classification as lore terminology.","sources":["original","storyboard"],"terms":["six","demons","arena"]}],"gallery":[{"src":"assets/archive/original/moon_ritual.webp","alt":"A ritual performed beneath the moon near a medieval village","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/ritual_chamber.webp","alt":"A figure standing in a candlelit ritual chamber","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/doll_relief.webp","alt":"The priest kneeling beside the discovered stone Relief","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/demon_arena.webp","alt":"Six demons facing a captive inside the Cult arena","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":true},{"src":"assets/archive/original/doll_close2.webp","alt":"The Doll standing in a moonlit forest","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/village_day.webp","alt":"A crowded medieval village street","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/hidden_village.webp","alt":"A timber hall occupied by antlered druidic warriors","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/city_night.webp","alt":"A guarded city street at night","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/cathedral_battle.webp","alt":"A vast gothic cathedral during a confrontation","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":true},{"src":"assets/archive/original/colosseum.webp","alt":"A ruined colosseum beyond autumn trees","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/sewer.webp","alt":"A torchlit sewer chamber beneath the city","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/flesh_cave.webp","alt":"A cavern transformed by flesh and forbidden magic","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":true},{"src":"assets/archive/original/ram_ruins.webp","alt":"A warrior confronting a horned enemy among ruins","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/royalty.webp","alt":"Kingdom royalty overlooking the city","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/moon_forest.webp","alt":"A towering antlered Wendigo stalking a moonlit forest","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/doll_beasts_night.webp","alt":"Corrupted animals around the Doll at night","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/doll_beasts_day.webp","alt":"The Doll seated near corrupted animals in daylight","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/doll_close1.webp","alt":"A close view of the Doll in a forest","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/original/monster_dinner.webp","alt":"A grotesque dinner-scene creature study","source":"Eclipsed Realms","kind":"Concept / visual-development reference","spoiler":true},{"src":"assets/archive/discover/cult-cathedral-facade.png","alt":"The supplied cult cathedral reference: a gothic entrance and rose window built between dark rock walls, illuminated by cold overhead light.","source":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","kind":"Supplied environment reference; original watermark retained","spoiler":false},{"src":"assets/archive/discover/cult-cathedral-approach.png","alt":"A high-angle supplied reference of the cult cathedral entrance, reached by a narrow bridge above a rocky chasm.","source":"Eclipsed Realms — Discover the Realm","kind":"Supplied environment reference; original watermark retained","spoiler":false}]};
